# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## What Was Done

### 1. Dependencies Installed
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1` using pnpm
- The package was already listed in package.json but node_modules needed to be installed

### 2. Content Security Policy Updated
Modified `app/source/index.html` to add Vercel Analytics domains to CSP:
- Added `https://va.vercel-scripts.com` to `script-src` directive
  - This allows Vercel to load the analytics script in production
- `https://vitals.vercel-insights.com` was already present in `connect-src`
  - This allows the analytics data to be sent to Vercel's servers

### 3. Analytics Script Configured
Updated `app/source/analytics.js` to use the recommended window.va stub pattern:
- Follows the official Vercel documentation for vanilla JavaScript/HTML projects
- The stub initializes `window.va` and queues events until the actual script loads
- Removed manual pageview tracking since Vercel Analytics automatically tracks pageviews
- When deployed to Vercel, their infrastructure will inject the actual analytics script

### 4. Build Verified
- Ran `npm run build` successfully
- Confirmed analytics.js is included in the generated HTML
- Confirmed CSP changes were properly propagated to the output

## Implementation Details

This project uses a vanilla JavaScript/HTML approach without a bundler. The implementation follows Vercel's recommended pattern for such projects:

1. **window.va stub pattern**: The analytics.js file creates a stub that queues analytics calls until the real script loads
2. **Automatic injection**: When deployed on Vercel, the platform automatically injects the production analytics script
3. **CSP compliance**: Updated the Content Security Policy to allow the analytics script and data transmission

## Files Modified

- `app/source/index.html` - Updated CSP to allow Vercel Analytics domains
- `app/source/analytics.js` - Refined the analytics initialization code to match latest docs

## Verification

The analytics will work automatically once deployed to Vercel. To verify:
1. Deploy the site to Vercel
2. Visit the deployed site
3. Check browser DevTools Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` or similar paths
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab

## Notes

- The analytics script is already included at the end of index.html (line 520)
- Analytics will only work on the Vercel-deployed version; local development won't send analytics data
- The window.va stub ensures no errors occur during local development when the actual script isn't present
